WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.208
[MUSIC]

00:00:06.208 --> 00:00:07.660
Hi, I'm Jennifer Aaker.

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:10.665
I'm a behavioral scientist who
spent my career, studying,

00:00:10.665 --> 00:00:13.800
what actually creates happiness and
life versus what we think.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:15.290
&gt;&gt; I'm Naomi Bagdonas.

00:00:15.290 --> 00:00:19.518
I'm a corporate strategist who spent my
career straddling the worlds of business

00:00:19.518 --> 00:00:21.988
and improv comedy,
which was a wide straddle.

00:00:21.988 --> 00:00:25.156
I'm Connor Diemand-Yauma,
a social entrepreneur and

00:00:25.156 --> 00:00:30.000
CEO who spent my career building vibrant,
productive, and humorous cultures.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.264
&gt;&gt; Together we teach a class called Humor,
Serious Business,

00:00:33.264 --> 00:00:35.510
about the power of humor and leadership.

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:38.126
It turns out humor is a teachable skill,
and

00:00:38.126 --> 00:00:41.840
it's one of the most under
appreciated assets at work.

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:46.022
&gt;&gt; Laughing changes the chemistry of
our brains making us more creative,

00:00:46.022 --> 00:00:47.426
bonded and resilient.

00:00:47.426 --> 00:00:51.752
Humor is an elixir for trust and
an antidote to arrogance, especially for

00:00:51.752 --> 00:00:53.210
today's leaders.

00:00:53.210 --> 00:00:54.580
&gt;&gt; But here's the problem.

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:56.520
We fallen off a humor cliff and

00:00:56.520 --> 00:01:01.860
global study over a million people
were asked a really simple question.

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:04.998
Did you smile or laugh the, yesterday?

00:01:04.998 --> 00:01:08.160
Now, as kids, we laugh all the time.

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:12.800
And then, right when we enter
the workforce, we stop laughing.

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:16.090
And we don't start laughing
again until we retire.

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:20.500
&gt;&gt; Which is why it's time to
start taking humor seriously.

00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:25.011
Here are five key takeaways from our
course to help you climb back up the humor

00:01:25.011 --> 00:01:27.848
cliff, add more humor at work and
in your life.

00:01:27.848 --> 00:01:31.219
[MUSIC]

00:01:31.219 --> 00:01:35.074
&gt;&gt; Our research reveals that there
are four broad humor styles and

00:01:35.074 --> 00:01:38.560
most people naturally fall into one or
two of them.

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:39.930
First is the stand up.

00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:44.187
Stand ups are bold natural entertainers
unafraid to ruffle a few feathers for

00:01:44.187 --> 00:01:45.530
a laugh.

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:46.660
Next is the sweetheart.

00:01:46.660 --> 00:01:51.700
Sweethearts are earnest, understated and
tend to use humor that lightens the mood.

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:57.390
Snipers are edgy, sarcastic, nuanced and
masters of the unexpected dig.

00:01:57.390 --> 00:01:58.830
Finally, there's the magnet.

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:02.700
Magnets are expressive, charismatic and
not afraid to be silly.

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:04.010
Once you know your style,

00:02:04.010 --> 00:02:07.653
you can start applying a few simple
techniques from the world of comedy.

00:02:07.653 --> 00:02:10.956
[MUSIC]

00:02:10.956 --> 00:02:15.725
&gt;&gt; To have more humor, start by making
simple observations throughout the day of

00:02:15.725 --> 00:02:19.260
things you find interesting,
odd, or amusing.

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:24.610
Since working from home,
I only calm the front part of my hair.

00:02:24.610 --> 00:02:29.979
Or I get really excited when people
cancel plans, isn't that the best?

00:02:29.979 --> 00:02:34.320
Or I wish there were a mute
button in real life.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:37.704
Now remember that this isn't
about becoming a comedian,

00:02:37.704 --> 00:02:41.570
it's about looking at
the world in a different way.

00:02:41.570 --> 00:02:45.190
Our brains are wired to find
what we set out to look for.

00:02:45.190 --> 00:02:47.124
So start looking for humor.

00:02:47.124 --> 00:02:50.390
[MUSIC]

00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:52.898
&gt;&gt; At work, it's easy to be transactional,

00:02:52.898 --> 00:02:56.321
but small shifts can move us
from transactional to human.

00:02:56.321 --> 00:03:00.436
As small as adding a light hearted line
at the end of your LinkedIn bio, or

00:03:00.436 --> 00:03:04.060
kicking off a meeting with
your favorite TED lasso clip.

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:07.170
Are you going to sign off
your emails with best?

00:03:07.170 --> 00:03:10.473
Instead, try something like yours,
heavily caffeinated or

00:03:10.473 --> 00:03:12.840
let's never speak of this again.

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:15.710
Or sometimes, I'm the best.

00:03:15.710 --> 00:03:17.343
Sometimes you just gotta let people know.

00:03:17.343 --> 00:03:20.802
[MUSIC]

00:03:20.802 --> 00:03:22.330
&gt;&gt; Humor can be risky risky.

00:03:22.330 --> 00:03:26.040
Here are a few things we tell our
students about how to de risk your humor.

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:29.820
First, don't ask will
this make me sound funny?

00:03:29.820 --> 00:03:33.150
Instead, ask how will this
make other people feel?

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:37.730
Which also means never punching down, that
is, making fun of someone of lower status.

00:03:37.730 --> 00:03:39.430
And be sure to check your distance.

00:03:39.430 --> 00:03:42.550
How close are you personally to
what you're making light of?

00:03:42.550 --> 00:03:46.393
I can make fun of my mother but
not Jennifer's mother who by the way,

00:03:46.393 --> 00:03:47.480
I hear is a saint.

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:49.410
&gt;&gt; She is a saint, thank you.

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:50.125
&gt;&gt; A lovely woman.

00:03:50.125 --> 00:03:53.828
[MUSIC]

00:03:53.828 --> 00:03:57.845
&gt;&gt; It's easy to believe that if you take
your life or your mission seriously,

00:03:57.845 --> 00:04:00.289
the presence of humor
betrays that mission.

00:04:00.289 --> 00:04:00.859
[MUSIC]

00:04:00.859 --> 00:04:05.930
As leaders of all stripes, from
secretary of State Madeleine Albright to

00:04:05.930 --> 00:04:10.933
NBA All Star Stephen Curry to
CEO Sara Blakely, tell a different story.

00:04:10.933 --> 00:04:16.200
That we can do serious things without
taking ourselves too seriously.

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:19.220
And in fact, often we can do them better.

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:22.836
&gt;&gt; Our hope is that you start climbing
back up the humor Cliff get to

00:04:22.836 --> 00:04:24.760
know your humor style.

00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:26.510
Mind your life for truth.

00:04:26.510 --> 00:04:29.910
Make small shifts from
transactional to human.

00:04:29.910 --> 00:04:31.232
Practice safe sets and

00:04:31.232 --> 00:04:35.680
make the choice to navigate your
life on the precipice of a smile.

00:04:35.680 --> 00:04:38.545
In other words,
start taking humor seriously.

00:04:38.545 --> 00:04:40.229
&gt;&gt; Seriously.

00:04:40.229 --> 00:04:40.851
&gt;&gt; Seriously.

00:04:40.851 --> 00:04:42.718
[LAUGH]

00:04:42.718 --> 00:04:49.578
[MUSIC]

00:04:49.578 --> 00:04:50.221
I love it.

00:04:50.221 --> 00:04:51.835
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]

